Z||000000||donny||11-04-2001||06:58 PM||||I'm so happy I finally got a gt and for the price of $750 a very nice one.Well here's the story.I went passed this used car lot a couple of times and see this beautiful 86 gt sitting there right by the service garage.Now I just traded in my 87 coupe last month.Didn't want to but it had high miles and the engine wasn't good.It was my first car but I had to let it go.So I got a nice 88 chrysler conquest tsi on credit and <BR>have been making payments.The conquest was really fast and was fully loaded with leather,a 5 speed and all that other good stuff.Well even though my conquest had over 200hp and was really fast and handled well it just didn't seem right.I found myself still on the fiero forum for hours at a time<BR>and wanting another fiero.So on thursday I stop at the lot with the gt and look it over and find out the guy got it in on a trade and didn't want to put another engine in it because to him it's just a fiero and he didn't want to bother.Now let me tell you this car is close to perfect in every way and loaded at that 64,000 original miles,red with grey ground effects,Fastback,<BR>spoiler,performance sound package,pw,pwd,tilt steering everything.||||reg||7
Z||000001||donny||11-04-2001||07:02 PM||||Oh yeah so my dad decided he would take over payments on the conquest(he loves that car)and I made a deposit on the gt yesterday and I'm picking it up monday.<BR>Just another thing that proves fieros are addictive.Sorry I took up so much space but I'm really excited.||||reg||7
Z||000002||8Ball||11-04-2001||07:13 PM||||He didn't want to put another engine in it?<P>Is the one in it blown?||||reg||1
Z||000003||donny||11-04-2001||07:18 PM||||Yeah it was knocking and having some other problems so he told me it would need another engine.He doesn't do engine swaps himself he has to send them out and I guess to him it is just taking up space.I'll post pics after I bring it home.Well after a nice washing and waxing of course.||||reg||1
